CONTEXT FROM TEXTBOOK:
This figure is a perspective line drawing of a rectangular coil rotating in a uniform magnetic field. The coil appears as a tall rectangular loop of several stacked turns, rendered as a striped gray band so the windings show, and tilted so its face is seen obliquely. A vertical axis labeled z passes through the coil's center, solid above and below the loop and dashed where it crosses the interior; a small circular arrow curls around its top to give the sense of rotation. A second axis labeled x runs diagonally toward the lower left, with a dashed segment continuing to the upper right. From the center point, a bold blue arrow labeled B points horizontally to the right as the uniform field, while an orange arrow labeled n-hat, the unit normal to the coil's surface, springs from the same origin and tilts down and to the right; a thin arc between the two marks the angle theta. Anchoring n-hat and B at a shared origin makes the angle between them the one quantity the reader tracks as the loop turns. The arrangement sets up the flux through a rotating coil and the emf that rotation induces.

PROJECTION TYPE: perspective
Use the scaffold's true perspective projection after building all geometry. Use this only when the source has real vanishing-point convergence or distance-based size shrinkage; then depth should visibly affect apparent size.

ELEMENTS TO RECREATE IN 3D:
  - tall rectangular coil loop drawn as a striped gray band of several stacked turns (multi-turn winding), face seen obliquely
  - vertical z-axis line through the coil center, solid above and below the loop, dashed where it passes behind/through the loop interior
  - 'z' label at top of vertical axis
  - small circular arrow curling around the top of the z-axis indicating rotation sense
  - diagonal x-axis running to lower-left with arrowhead, plus dashed continuation to upper-right through the loop
  - 'x' label at lower-left end of the diagonal axis
  - short horizontal y-axis segment extending to the left of the origin
  - origin point at the center of the coil where all vectors are anchored
  - bold blue arrow pointing horizontally to the right from the origin, labeled 'B' with vector overbar
  - orange arrow from the origin tilting down and to the right, the unit normal, labeled 'n̂'
  - thin arc between the blue B arrow and the orange n̂ arrow with 'θ' label
  - flux/emf readout text (Φ = BA cos θ, ε = NBAω sin θ)
